The Nautilus DevOps team wants to install and set up a simple httpd web server on all app servers in Stratos DC. Additionally, they want to deploy a sample web page for now using Ansible only. Therefore, write the required playbook to complete this task. Find more details about the task below.
We already have an inventory file under /home/thor/ansible directory on jump host. Create a playbook.yml under /home/thor/ansible directory on jump host itself.
Using the playbook, install httpd web server on all app servers. Additionally, make sure its service should up and running.
Using blockinfile Ansible module add some content in /var/www/html/index.html file. Below is the content:
Welcome to XfusionCorp!
This is  Nautilus sample file, created using Ansible!
Please do not modify this file manually!
The /var/www/html/index.html file's user and group owner should be apache on all app servers.
The /var/www/html/index.html file's permissions should be 0744 on all app servers.


Note:
i. Validation will try to run the playbook using command ansible-playbook -i inventory playbook.yml so please make sure the playbook works this way without passing any extra arguments.
ii. Do not use any custom or empty marker for blockinfile module.

SOLUTION
Create /home/thor/ansible/playbook.yml with this:

---
- name: Install and configure httpd on all app servers
  hosts: all
  become: true


  tasks:
    - name: Install httpd
      ansible.builtin.yum:
        name: httpd
        state: present


    - name: Ensure httpd is running and enabled
      ansible.builtin.service:
        name: httpd
        state: started
        enabled: true


    - name: Add sample content to index.html
      ansible.builtin.blockinfile:
        path: /var/www/html/index.html
        create: true
        block: |
          Welcome to XfusionCorp!


          This is  Nautilus sample file, created using Ansible!


          Please do not modify this file manually!


    - name: Set ownership and permissions on index.html
      ansible.builtin.file:
        path: /var/www/html/index.html
        owner: apache
        group: apache
        mode: '0744'

Then run exactly as the validator will:

cd /home/thor/ansible
ansible-playbook -i inventory playbook.yml
Verify
ansible -i inventory all -m shell -a "systemctl is-active httpd && ls -l /var/www/html/index.html && cat /var/www/html/index.html"

The important details are:

hosts: all — works with the existing inventory.
become: true — required for package/service/web-root changes.
blockinfile uses its default markers; no custom or empty marker is specified.
Owner/group are both apache.
Permissions are exactly 0744.
